# Site Structure & Content Specification for "My Blog Desk"

**Repository:** `blog-evd`  
**Site Identity:** DeepaRam — Painting Emotions in Stillness  
**Target User:** Non-technical mobile companion app ("My Blog Desk") publishing content via GitHub Contents API commits triggering Vercel auto-deploys.  
**Report Date:** November 2026  

---

> [!CAUTION]
> ### CRITICAL ARCHITECTURAL FINDING
> **The entire repository currently hardcodes 100% of its content directly inside TypeScript React component files (`.tsx`)**.
> 
> There is **no `content/` directory**, **no Markdown/MDX parser**, **no frontmatter extractor (`gray-matter`)**, **no CMS**, and **no JSON data loader**.
> 
> If a companion app commits a Markdown, MDX, or JSON content file to this repository today, **Next.js will not read it, parse it, or display it**. For the "My Blog Desk" model (committing content files only without touching code) to function, a **content loader abstraction** (reading from local JSON or Markdown files via `fs` or a parser) must be introduced into the site code, or the companion app must be aware of the exact `.tsx` data structures.
> 
> Full details and transition specifications are documented in **Section 3**, **Section 6**, and **Section 7**.

